# The ARCHITECTURAL WITNESS TIER -- one representative case per execution
# class (declared 2026-08-10, Vitor's testing-hierarchy ruling).
#
# WHAT THIS IS.  `bin/runTests --witnesses` runs exactly these cases through
# the SAME checks as the full sweep (NaN/inf guard, golden-master KPIs,
# anchor rows) and answers, in minutes:
#
#     does each major simulator class still traverse the architecture?
#
# The FULL 459-case regression answers a different question -- "did we break
# any historical case?" -- and is reserved for campaign closure, releases and
# genuinely cross-cutting changes.  Using it as the routine feedback loop was
# the defect this tier exists to end.  The ladder is recorded in
# docs/architecture/verification-and-validation.md.
#
# A WITNESS IS A ROLE, NOT A MORADA.  These cases stay where they live; the
# tier is this declaration, exactly as a component's category lives inside
# its record (components/ stays flat) and a stream's role is inferred from
# topology.  A case may be a teaching tutorial AND a witness -- what is
# refused is complicating a tutorial to serve witnessing, or minting a
# duplicate case for a role an existing case already carries.
#
# EACH LINE: <class>  <case path>.  One class, one case.  The tier is kept
# SMALL on purpose -- a witness earns its line by traversing the full
# architectural route its class depends on, never by ticking boxes with
# physically irrelevant machinery.  Gate: check_witness_tier (existence,
# golden, class uniqueness; it does NOT judge representativeness -- that is
# an architect's call, made here, in review).
#
